									</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/grigori-karpin" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4558017); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4558017&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608104641" alt="Grigori Karpin" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4558017)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/grigori-karpin" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4558017); return false;" >Grigori Karpin</a></span> <span class="odate time_1608102906 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">16 Dec 2020 07:15</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13912704/deus-comedenti-translation:god-eater">Deus Comedenti (Translation: God Eater)</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4845956">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Something that bugs me about this concept is that it seems to be including widespread murder of homeless or prisoners merely for an easy excuse to have a moral dilemma. That seems excessively grimdark for the sake of easy horror - <em>&quot;over the top&quot; in terms of violence just for the sake of &quot;isn't that scary?&quot;</em></p>
<p>I'm also not full convinced on the whole <em>this machine was built to eat gods but now it eats humans</em> and also <em>that anything that was designed WAY back in prehistory to kill gods wouldn't be likely to convert them into electricity</em>.</p>
<p>Moreover, I think you're still missing a narrative arc here. What is the story about? Just a discussion of this magical god killing machine and its history, isn't really a story. Neither is just presenting a dilemma like &quot;Should the government be sacrificing the poor for benefit of the rich?&quot; (which is btw what you're saying)</p>
<p>Narratives need more than a dilemma. Where is the conflict? Characters? plot, etc?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
I think you should consider these things, and if you don't want to change the proposal, consider reaching out to other reviewers to see if maybe its just me.
							</div>

								
					
